    "title": "Congress should pass the Parents Over Platforms Act | Harrison County Letters to the Editor | wvnews.com",
    "text": "The recent news about Meta settling with 47 states, including ours, and paying $17 billion in penalties for all the harm it’s caused kids was good news. That being said, Congress still needs to do its job and pass laws that force Meta and other social media platforms to do more to keep kids safe.\nI just learned a bill in the United States Senate would help us keep our kids safe by telling every app on a phone, at once, that a child is the one using it.",
